      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Courts usually look at the \"substance\" of the resemblance, determining if the specific, non-obvious elements of the protected information were incorporated. If the logic is merely a standard algorithmic solution to a common problem, it's likely safe; however, if your logic mirrors a unique, non-public approach they developed, it raises a red flag. The actual threshold often depends on how closely your implementation maps to their specific, confidential solution, even if the core idea seems generic.",
